From 409a75bb26d6b1398c5aeefe57a4490f870e7494 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:00:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nak: scoreboard sharing and SM120 latency padding knobs for
 hardware validation (NAK_BAR_SHARE, NAK_LAT)

Both default to off; they exist to be validated on hardware (naktest) and
measured before any of it is turned on.

NAK_BAR_SHARE=1: when all six scoreboards are in use, a new
variable-latency instruction joins the scoreboard used most recently
instead of first waiting for the oldest one to finish.  A scoreboard then
tracks several instructions, and waiting on it waits for all of them.  In
the heavy Steel Nomad shaders 215-389 instructions issue with all six
scoreboards pending.

NAK_LAT (bitmask): leaves out the blanket one extra cycle of the SM120 RAW
latencies for pairs where the stall counts of NVIDIA's public ptxas
(-arch=sm_120) on probe PTX use the SM100 latency: 1 FMA-class chains,
2 FMA/ALU cross pairs, 4 predicate guards, 8 coupled carry predicates,
16 uniform datapath, 64 LOP3/PRMT/SHF chains, 128 every pair (unsafe upper
bound).

Both are part of nak_knobs_key().
---
 src/nouveau/compiler/nak/calc_instr_deps.rs   | 70 ++++++++++++-----
 src/nouveau/compiler/nak/knobs.rs             | 36 ++++++++-
 .../compiler/nak/sm120_instr_latencies.rs     | 77 ++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 161 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

